

%%{init: {
  'flowchart': {
    'curve': 'linear',
    'direction': 'TB',
    'nodeSpacing': 250,
    'rankSpacing': 120,
    'padding': 15
  }
}}%

flowchart TB

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Bid / ITB Review
%% ===============================
subgraph L1["Bid / ITB Review"]
direction TB
A["ITB and Design Basis Review<br/><br/>
1. Telecom design basis and philosophy reviewed<br/>
2. Telecom specifications and block diagrams reviewed<br/>
3. Indoor and outdoor IP ratings confirmed<br/>
4. Hazardous-area and explosion-proof requirements confirmed<br/>
5. Codes standards and local regulations confirmed<br/>
6. Security regulations confirmed for example Saudi HCIS
"]

B["Scope Interfaces and Existing Systems<br/><br/>
1. Supply and work scope boundaries defined<br/>
2. Expansion and modification interfaces identified<br/>
3. Tie-in points and physical connections identified<br/>
4. Intra-system and inter-system interfaces checked<br/>
5. Existing system capacity and IO ports verified<br/>
6. Site survey requirement confirmed
"]

C["Redundancy and Reliability Requirements<br/><br/>
1. Hot standby and cold standby requirements verified<br/>
2. Failover load balancing one-plus-one and N-plus-one verified<br/>
3. Cable redundancy and route diversity verified<br/>
4. SIL-level security requirements verified<br/>
5. Single-system design applied where no requirement exists
"]

D["Default Subsystem Standards If ITB Is Silent<br/><br/>
1. Telephone standard defined SIP or H.323<br/>
2. CCTV standard defined IP-based H.264 1080p<br/>
3. PAGA standard defined 100V line Class C amplifier<br/>
4. Radio standard defined TETRA Release 2<br/>
5. ACS standard defined ISO IEC 18000-3 13.56 MHz<br/>
6. Firewall standard defined NIST 800-41<br/>
7. IDPS standard defined NIST 800-94
"]

A --> B --> C --> D
end

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Telecom System Design
%% ===============================
subgraph L2["Telecom System Design"]
direction TB

T["Telephone System Design<br/><br/>
1. Analog or VoIP system selected<br/>
2. MDF-IDF hierarchy applied for analog system<br/>
3. MDF-IDF trunk sized with spare capacity<br/>
4. VoIP patch panel ports sized with spare<br/>
5. Explosion-proof phones applied<br/>
6. Outdoor phone IP rating checked
"]

CCTV["CCTV System Design<br/><br/>
1. Resolution IPS traffic and storage defined<br/>
2. Default H.264 1080p applied if unspecified<br/>
3. IP rating and sunshade checked<br/>
4. Explosion-proof camera applied if required
"]

P["PAGA System Design<br/><br/>
1. Coverage requirement reviewed<br/>
2. Full area coverage applied if unspecified<br/>
3. A-B zoning applied where required<br/>
4. Speaker type selected by area and noise
"]

R["Radio System Design<br/><br/>
1. Coverage and licensing responsibility confirmed<br/>
2. Antenna height and coverage checked<br/>
3. Repeater applied only if signal below threshold
"]

ACS["Access Control System Design<br/><br/>
1. Door types classified<br/>
2. Reader application defined<br/>
3. Controller and IO cabling defined
"]

DN["Data Network and IDS Design<br/><br/>
1. Dual 1 Gbps redundancy applied if unspecified<br/>
2. Core distribution and access layers defined<br/>
3. Firewall and IDPS included where required
"]

D --> T
D --> CCTV
D --> P
D --> R
D --> ACS
D --> DN
end

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Quantity & Cable Engineering
%% ===============================
subgraph L3["Quantity and Cable Engineering"]
direction TB

F["Cable Rules and MTO Development<br/><br/>
1. Cable MTO derived from block diagrams and layouts<br/>
2. Telecom routes separated from electrical routes<br/>
3. Default cable types applied per system<br/>
4. Redundancy impact on quantities checked
"]

T --> F
CCTV --> F
P --> F
R --> F
ACS --> F
DN --> F
end

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Vendor & Interfaces
%% ===============================
subgraph L4["Vendor and Interfaces"]
direction TB

G["Vendor Scope and Interfaces<br/><br/>
1. Vendor-supplied items identified<br/>
2. Vendor scope included in MR and BOQ<br/>
3. Vendor quantities verified during TBE
"]

F --> G
end

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Interdiscipline
%% ===============================
subgraph L5["Interdiscipline Engineering"]
direction TB

H["Interdiscipline Engineering Deliverables<br/><br/>
1. Cable tray loading and routing issued to Civil<br/>
2. Trench and foundation data issued to Civil<br/>
3. Heat dissipation issued to HVAC<br/>
4. Grounding targets issued to Electrical
"]

G --> H
end

%% ===============================
%% Swimlane: Final Review & Control
%% ===============================
subgraph L6["Final Review and Control"]
direction TB

I["Vendor Packages and BOQ Validation<br/><br/>
1. Vendor issue package prepared and issued<br/>
2. Vendor return package reviewed<br/>
3. BOQ validated against vendor quantities<br/>
4. Revamp and tie-in quantities separated
"]

J["Final Estimate-Design Review<br/><br/>
1. AG and UG cable routing verified<br/>
2. Cable derating factors confirmed<br/>
3. ITB addenda confirmed incorporated<br/>
4. Estimate-design frozen for bid submission
"]

H --> I --> J
end
